# Base origin of the Next.js app that serves /api/plan.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the shipped JS bundle by Metro at build time and
# is readable by anyone who unzips the IPA/APK. It may hold a public URL. It must
# never hold an API key, token or any other secret.
#
# Local development: your dev machine's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:3000
# Anything shipped: must be https:// — this request carries face photos.
#
# When unset, fetchPlan() returns null and the app runs its local safety-engine
# demo instead. That is the default, and it means a release build with this unset
# silently never calls the real pipeline. Set it per build profile in eas.json.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
